3139	  /// Two carries whose buffers overlap cannot both survive an iteration: whatever
3140	  /// order the writebacks run in, the second one destroys the first. The usual
3141	  /// source is seeding two `pl.range` carries from one tile (`lag1 = one;
3142	  /// lag2 = one`), which makes both carries that tile's buffer. That is a real
3143	  /// limitation of the carry lowering rather than a compiler invariant, so it is
3144	  /// reported to the author -- and reported here, where the carries are still
3145	  /// named, rather than downstream as a degenerate `tile.move` onto itself.
