3700	
3701	  // Under memory_planner=PtoAS or DsaRP the whole MemoryReuse pass is skipped.
3702	  // DsaRP must therefore run the correctness normalizations from MemoryReuse
3703	  // Steps 3.75 through 4.5 in the same order. They are not optimizations: when a
3704	  // peeled accumulator if-phi or
3705	  // loop yields a value living in a different buffer than its iter_arg/return_var,
3706	  // it inserts the `tile.move` that writes the result back into the carry. Without
3707	  // it the carry is never updated and the loop silently becomes a no-op — the
3708	  // `[N, 1]` col-vector carry of an online softmax is the shape that hits this,
3709	  // because its branch producer runs on a `[1, N]` view in its own buffer.
3710	  //
3711	  // Run it here so both alternative planners reconcile carries. Under the
3712	  // legacy PyPTO planner it stays where it is: Step 4 must run *after* reuse
3713	  // decisions, which can themselves create fresh mismatches.
3714	  //
3715	  // PTOAS needs only the ForStmt YieldFixup half: addr-less codegen already
3716	  // re-points a branch-local producer at the if-phi handle. DSA-RP emits
3717	  // explicit addresses, so it must first coalesce peeled accumulator if-phis,
3718	  // then materialize both IfStmt and ForStmt fixups, and finally repair bare-Var
