3822	  // does not reconcile them with an illegal Acc->Acc tile.move.  See
3823	  // TopDownRetargeter::CoalesceAccumulatorIfPhis.  Must run after all ForStmt-carry
3824	  // coalescing (Steps 0/3/3.5) so the accumulator branch is on its final buffer, and
3825	  // before YieldFixupMutator (Step 4) so it observes one buffer per phi.  A no-op when
3826	  // no accumulator if-phi exists (e.g. non-pipelined kernels).
3827	  {
3828	    TopDownRetargeter acc_coalescer;
3829	    auto acc_rewrites = acc_coalescer.CoalesceAccumulatorIfPhis(new_body);
3830	    if (!acc_rewrites.empty()) {
3831	      RetypeApplier applier(std::move(acc_rewrites));
3832	      new_body = applier.VisitStmt(new_body);
3833	    }
3834	  }
3835	
3836	  // Step 3.9 / 4.5: Reconcile bare-Var SSA identity copies whose buffers diverged
3837	  // from the value they rename.  No-op when no mismatch exists.
3838	  //
3839	  // This runs on both sides of YieldFixup because both sides create such a
3840	  // divergence, from opposite directions:
3841	  //
3842	  //  - before, because Step 3.75's accumulator-if-phi retarget leaves a rename
3843	  //    stranded on the pre-coalesce buffer, and because a carry rename such as
3844	  //    `lag2 = lag1` only lands on lag1's buffer here. YieldFixup has to see the
3845	  //    settled buffer to order the carry writebacks against each other: against
3846	  //    the pre-normalization buffers every rename still sits on a buffer of its
3847	  //    own, so no conflict is visible and a shift register silently collapses
3848	  //    ([#2481]).
3849	  //  - after, because YieldFixup's own IfStmt fixup repoints a phi return_var
3850	  //    onto the canonical branch buffer, which strands that phi's downstream
3851	  //    `c = c_phi` rename in exactly the same way.
3852	  //
3853	  // The mutator is idempotent, so the second run is a no-op whenever the first
3854	  // already settled everything.
